  "why": "The paper's fuzzer and testing framework are not designed specifically to target or bypass deployed safeguards (e.g., detectors or adversarially-defended models); rather, RobOT is explicitly aimed at generating test cases that improve model robustness via retraining. However, the authors do empirically generate adversarial examples against models that have been retrained/enhanced (i.e., models with defenses in the form of robustness-enhancing retraining) and evaluate robustness on those models (showing adversarial examples exist for the retrained, more robust models). Thus the work demonstrates successful safeguard bypasses (adversarial examples against defended/retrained models) without having designed the failure oracle or mutation strategies specifically to discover such bypasses.",
